{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413525-octavio-tc","id":1413525,"title":"Octavio (TC)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T04:40:39-07:00","id":1413525,"title":"Octavio (TC)","content":"This Is quiet simple guys, hopefully you can help me again!<br /> <br /> Octavio character sheet Is presented in TC book. It says he has Nature and Demeanor: Prophet.<br /> I searched for Prophet archetype but apparently it does not exist. I searched for every book i have... Do you know were Prophet archetype Is described?<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for your help guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26189-wuzaolover","name":"WuZaolover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26189_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T04:57:56-07:00","id":1413530,"title":"","content":"In a sense, the Nature and Demeanour of an NPC doesn't actually need to be described, as NPCs don't (or shouldn't) gain a mechanical benefit out of these traits, as they exist for narrative purposes. Being able to understand what the writers mean is sufficient. That said, it's not ideal design to give NPCs traits that are not available to players, and are not actually described in rulebooks, as it does somewhat undermine the coherence of the game world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T05:01:37-07:00","id":1413531,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a> Sense and Sensibility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T05:08:58-07:00","id":1413535,"title":"","content":"So you actually do confirm me that the Prophet archetype has never been described but It has been used in an official sourcebook for a key NPC. Great. XD<br /> I Need It in order to Understand when exactly you regain willpower with the Prophet Nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26189-wuzaolover","name":"WuZaolover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26189_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T05:14:09-07:00","id":1413539,"title":"","content":"When your prophecies come true<br /> <br /> Or just change it to Visionary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T05:31:52-07:00","id":1413540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413525-octavio-tc?p=1413539#post1413539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just change it to Visionary</div> </div> </div> </div>You beat me to it.<br /> <br /> You may also consider the Seer archetype from LS4: Thieves in the Night. Though, by the time Anatole eats him, the Fatalist one from Victorian Age Vampire may be more fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-14-2020, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T22:07:24-07:00","id":1413709,"title":"","content":"There is a Prophet archetype on page 272 of Mage 20th Anniversary Edition. Essentially, the Prophet thinks they speak Truth with a capital 'T.' They have strong insight, like a Visionary, which is their strength. The flaw of a Prophet is their Ruthlessness. A Prophet regains Willpower by speaking their truth to power.<br /> <br /> Below is the most current edition of the archetypes list from the World of Darkness game lines.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Archetypes\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Archetypes</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}